hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17609","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, who said: A man from among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sham will be opened for you, so when you are given choice of dwellings therein, then upon you is a city called Damascus, for it is the stronghold of the Muslims against the great battles, and its encampment is in a land called al-Ghutah."
